          "Identify and address the 6% demographic gap: the ~2,800–3,500 residents not captured in the four Census categories represent a constituency whose civic participation and economic concerns are invisible in standard analysis but potentially consequential if mobilized; passive assumption of their voting behavior is a risk in a district this tightly margined.",
          "Do not campaign MA-1 as a safe Republican seat: a 56% result in a district with 44.9% college attainment and $88,902 income should yield a 60%+ Republican margin; the 4-percentage-point underperformance relative to demographic expectation suggests specific governance failures or swing-voter concerns that require active remedy, not confidence.",
