          { name: "Taking the Homeowner Majority for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "The 14.9% renter rate and high homeownership suggest a base that should produce a comfortable Republican margin — yet the incumbent held the opposition to 44%, indicating that homeowner loyalty is not automatic. Any candidate who campaigns this seat as though homeowners' material interests are aligned with Republican positioning without addressing their specific economic concerns — healthcare costs, property tax fairness, aging infrastructure — will find that the base does not consolidate at the margins, and modest persuasion among cost-conscious affluent voters becomes the difference between holding and losing." }
