          "Defend property tax fairness and the tax burden on middle-class homeowners: at 79.2% homeownership and $86,029 income, this is a constituency for whom property tax and state income tax directly shape disposable income and retirement security—and where the Republican opposition's tax-burden messaging can gain traction if Davis's record on tax policy is not actively defended.",
          "Address the college-educated professional constituency's quality-of-life priorities: public education funding, environmental protection, and labor standards are the non-partisan issues where educated, affluent voters in MA-03 evaluate performance—and where Davis's alignment with these priorities reinforces the 57% margin among professionals and public-sector workers.",
          "Monitor the 43% Republican floor for signs of consolidation: a 57% margin is safe only if it does not shrink; specific tracking of older homeowner satisfaction with healthcare and tax policy, and of younger adult outmigration, will reveal whether the base is eroding before a challenger can capitalize on the trend."
