          "Engage the 19%+ minority communities with specific policy attention rather than assumed loyalty; the Hispanic, Black, and Asian residents of Bristol County have distinct economic concerns around education funding, healthcare access, and housing affordability that deserve direct constituent outreach and legislative focus.",
          "Lead on housing affordability and education funding as the primary district-level issues; with 34.1% renters and 32.5% college-educated residents, younger adults and families are evaluating on whether state policy is supporting homeownership accessibility and school quality — these are the material concerns that could activate an opposition challenge.",
