          "Maintain active engagement with the Latino and immigrant communities that comprise 19.25% of the district; this constituency's economic vulnerability on wages, workplace protections, and housing costs makes them natural Democratic voters, but only if the incumbent is actively serving their material needs rather than taking their support as assured.",
          "Build relationship with the unaccounted-for 13.3% of the population: this gap likely represents immigrant, undocumented, and other marginalized communities whose civic participation and turnout are contingent on perceiving the incumbent as actively advocating for their interests, not treating them as demographic appendages.",
          "Do not campaign this seat as permanently safe: the unopposed 2024 result reflects absence of Republican opposition, not invulnerability. A working-class, renter-majority, 37.4-year-old constituency evaluates on concrete delivery—an incumbent who loses focus on the daily economic pressures of renters and working families creates an opening for either Republican challenger recruitment or primary competition from the left."
