          { name: "Assuming Partisan Loyalty Among High-Income, Educated Voters", tag: "avoid", why: "At $113,907 median income and 50.7% college attainment, MA-1st Essex voters are affluent and educated enough to evaluate representatives on individual merit and specific policy delivery rather than partisan default. This constituency cares about fiscal management, education quality, infrastructure, and whether government is delivering tangible results. Any candidate—incumbent or challenger—who campaigns on partisan affiliation alone rather than concrete constituent outcomes is underestimating the sophistication and independence of voters in this district. An incumbent secure in her Democratic registration but perceived as ineffective or invisible is significantly more vulnerable than the unopposed result suggests." }
