          { name: "Treating Racial and Ethnic Communities as Decorative Rather Than Constituent", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district that is 81.11% white, the 6.92% Hispanic, 4.43% Asian, and 2.99% Black communities can easily become incorporated into an incumbent's electoral strategy as symbolic gestures rather than constituencies with specific governance needs. Token appearances at community events without demonstrable policy attention to immigration, healthcare access, educational equity, or economic mobility in immigrant communities reads to those constituencies as indifference — and a challenger who addresses these issues with specificity and legislative action can mobilize them quickly, potentially shifting the district's competitive dynamics in a single cycle." }
