          "Lead with housing affordability and renter constituency engagement: at 39.5% renter rate and $90,343 median income, a substantial portion of the district faces cost-of-living pressure that affluent homeowners do not experience—and housing policy, rental protections, and development decisions directly affect constituent economic security.",
          "Build authentic relationships with the growing Hispanic/Latino (14.18%), Black (4.14%), and Asian (1.92%) communities through specific constituent service and legislative attention to their distinct economic and social concerns, not generic minority outreach—the unopposed result means these communities' needs have not been tested or surfaced in electoral competition.",
          "Avoid the trap of treating a 100-0 result as evidence of permanent Democratic dominance: demographic change, economic pressure on renters, and generational shifts in younger adults' political alignment mean that complacency about this seat's security is strategically dangerous over a five-to-ten-year horizon."
