          { name: "Neglecting Higher Education Affordability & Workforce Access", tag: "avoid", why: "At 56.5% college attainment, this is a district where higher education access and cost are lived household concerns for parents with college-age children and for younger adults evaluating career pathways. An incumbent whose legislative record on education affordability and public higher education funding is weak or unclear will appear misaligned with a constituency whose material stakes in education quality extend beyond K-12 into college access and workforce development for their children." }
