          "Treat unopposed 2024 victory as a governance mandate, not electoral security—maintain relentless constituent service infrastructure, respond to service requests with documented speed and resolution, and build documented relationships with school committees, municipal officials, and civic organizations that generate grassroots defense against challenger credibility claims.",
          "Lead on school funding adequacy and property tax fairness with specificity: at $131,663 income in a district where school quality directly affects property values and retirement decisions, education funding and tax policy are the material governance concerns that drive incumbent approval or vulnerability to a challenger positioning on fiscal competence.",
