          { name: "Assuming Partisan Loyalty in an Affluent Swing Demographic", tag: "avoid", why: "Affluent, college-educated suburban districts — particularly those with growing Hispanic populations — are the most ideologically flexible constituencies in modern politics and the most capable of shifting between parties based on candidate quality and issue salience. A representative who assumes this district will hold based on partisan label rather than on sustained delivery of competent governance, responsive constituent service, and integration of the growing Hispanic community into positions of economic and civic influence is misreading the actual dynamics of high-income suburban politics." }
