          { name: "Ignoring the Renter Plurality's Needs in a Homeowner-Centric Campaign", tag: "avoid", why: "While homeowners dominate at 73.3%, the 26.7% renter population — roughly one in four households — represents a material constituency whose economic needs (housing, childcare, wage-work stability) are distinct from property-owner concerns. A Whipps campaign that treats renters as an afterthought or assumes they are not politically engaged will create an opening for a challenger who can offer specific responses to rental affordability and working-family economic security. In a district with 34% opposition, leaving 27% of households feeling unserved is a strategic error." }
