          "The 66% result in a demographically homogeneous district with no significant racial or ethnic diversity and moderate college attainment (27.4%) is not a dominant margin — it is a consolidated plurality that leaves 34% of the electorate actively open to an alternative. Treat this as a persuadable constituency, not a locked Republican base.",
