          "Lead with aging homeowner economic security: property tax fairness, healthcare cost control, and state fiscal discipline are the material concerns of a 47.5-year-old, 80% homeowner, $90,530 median-income constituency. Articulate specific, legislative remedies rather than generic conservative positioning.",
          "Recognize that 35.5% college attainment is below Massachusetts state average and signals a constituency with less credential-driven economic mobility — healthcare workers, trades, public employees, and small business owners vulnerable to cost-of-living pressure. These voters evaluate on whether government is delivering tangible fiscal responsibility and service quality, not partisan identity.",
          "Build constituent infrastructure that captures homeowner frustration on property taxes, healthcare, and state spending before a challenger can weaponize it. Unopposed victories can breed legislative complacency; active constituent engagement is the foundation of durability in a district where 80% of households have real economic stakes in fiscal policy."
