          "Address renter households' economic security directly: at 40.4% renters and $67k median income, housing affordability, tenant protections, and access to public transportation are material quality-of-life issues that shape whether younger and lower-income voters stay engaged or become vulnerable to an alternative.",
          "Build year-round constituent service infrastructure in Spanish-language community organizations, small business associations, and neighborhood groups; an unopposed victory is an opportunity to deepen constituent relationships, not permission to govern from a distance.",
          "Monitor competitor emergence closely: the absence of opposition in 2024 does not indicate lack of interest from potential challengers, particularly if they perceive genuine gaps between the incumbent and Latino or renter-majority voters; invest in constituent relationships before a credible opponent materializes."
