          "Build active relationships with the 16% Hispanic/Latino and 7.5% Black communities: these populations in an affluent suburban district can become invisible in representation and service delivery; attention to their economic mobility, educational access, and healthcare concerns is both constituent service and electoral insurance against a challenger who makes these communities visible.",
          "Document and communicate constituent service metrics and legislative outcomes: unopposed victories create the false impression of an invincible incumbent; the next challenger will likely run on governance failure rather than ideology, so building a record of responsiveness, constituent service, and specific legislative accomplishments is the most durable defense against future opposition."
