          "Engage the college-educated majority on education and infrastructure: 48% college attainment signals a constituency that prioritizes school quality, higher education access, and the public investments that maintain community desirability. Specific commitments on education funding, university affordability, and infrastructure maintenance are far more persuasive than abstract partisan messaging in a district where quality of life is the primary evaluation metric.",
          "Address the 49% opposition directly: understand whether it stems from fiscal concerns (perceived Democratic overspending), service quality concerns (infrastructure or school performance), or ideological preference — and offer concrete governance remedies rather than assuming the 51% is a stable base. A 2-point margin is razor-thin; any candidate must treat the opposition as a persuadable constituency, not a permanent opposition.",
