          "Maintain active constituent engagement with the district's 10.5% Asian American community and 3.9% Hispanic community; at median ages and income levels consistent with more recent immigrant or first-generation professional families, these constituencies have distinct policy concerns around education access, health equity, and economic opportunity that deserve specific legislative attention rather than absorption into the white professional-class narrative.",
          "Monitor for any erosion of the 73% Democratic consensus through targeted polling on education funding adequacy, property tax fairness, and whether the representative is perceived as delivering tangible results for the district; supermajorities can invert rapidly if an incumbent loses credibility with the professional-class base around education or property-tax management."
