          "Target the 24.5% renter minority directly: younger professionals and service workers in this affluent district face housing cost pressure and may be responsive to messages about housing affordability, wage growth, and economic mobility that the Democratic incumbent may not be emphasizing to the homeowner majority.",
          "Build credibility on fiscal management and municipal service delivery rather than abstract ideology—a 64.1% college-educated constituency at $148,838 income evaluates on competence and results, not partisan label. Any challenger must articulate a specific case that Day's governance has failed on measurable outcomes where affluent suburban voters care most.",
