          { name: "Treating Unopposed 2024 Result as Confirmation of Permanent Safety", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed win in 2024 reflects current Republican Party strategic calculations in Democratic Massachusetts, not the permanent electoral architecture of the district. Suburban Massachusetts districts with growing renter populations, demographic diversification, and material economic concerns about housing and education are not immune to Republican challenge if resources are deployed and messaging is responsive to constituent frustration. Complacency about the unopposed result is the primary threat to long-term seat durability." },
          { name: "Defaulting Governance to Homeowner Interests While Neglecting Renter Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "A representative who prioritizes property tax management and education funding for homeowner constituencies while treating rental affordability and tenant protection as secondary issues is not governing the actual district. With 35.8% renters, a governance approach that serves only the 64% homeowner majority fractures the constituency and creates opening for opposition to consolidate renter frustration. Durable representation requires explicit service to both populations simultaneously." }
