          "Treat the unopposed 2024 result as a vulnerability signal, not confirmation of safety: unopposed status in one cycle does not guarantee durability if constituent engagement lapses or if a credible challenger emerges; proactive constituent service and visible legislative accomplishment on housing and education are the foundation for holding this seat in a future contested race.",
          "Develop specific legislative agenda on education funding, property tax fairness, and public infrastructure that resonates with the 43.4% college-educated, homeowner-majority base while explicitly addressing renter economic concerns: this is the constituency that actually lives in Massachusetts' 4th Norfolk, and governance that serves both populations simultaneously is more durable than governance that defaults to homeowner interests."
