          "Engage the 19.5% Asian community with specific policy attention and authentic constituent relationship-building — this is a meaningful demographic plurality within the non-white community whose concerns around education quality, healthcare access, small business policy, and immigration-adjacent issues deserve direct representation rather than absorption into a generic 'communities of color' narrative.",
          "Do not treat unopposed status as permission to govern passively; a district with 46.2% college attainment and $124K median income will mobilize a credible challenger if the incumbent appears inattentive to constituent concerns or if specific policy decisions create concentrated opposition — the absence of a 2024 challenger is not evidence of a safe seat, only of current Democratic lean.",
          "Address the renter community (22.3%) specifically around housing affordability, tenant protections, and whether local zoning policy serves younger adults and moderate-income renters or only protects single-family homeowner interests — this constituency can swing the district if they perceive the representative as indifferent to their housing costs and security."
