          "Lead with local governance performance on schools, property tax burden, and public safety: the white, college-educated, homeowner-majority base of the district is fiscally conservative relative to Democratic Party orthodoxy and evaluates on schools, safety, and tax efficiency. Specific wins on school funding equity, police accountability that maintains community confidence, and property tax management are the constituency service measures that consolidate the affluent base against a fiscal-conservative challenger.",
          "Build explicit relationships with Black and Asian communities around their distinct policy priorities: do not assume that race-based Democratic solidarity automatically holds this 15.73% + 8.23% = 24% of the district. Criminal justice reform, affirmative action, education access for first-generation students, and immigration policy have different valences and urgency for Black and Asian voters. Active constituent listening and specific legislative alignment on these issues is required to hold these communities' engagement and turnout.",
