          "Address the specific economic pressures of a $131,823-income constituency whose wealth can mask real anxiety about children's education costs, healthcare premiums, and property tax sustainability — treating affluence as a proxy for contentment is a mistake.",
          "Build authentic relationships with professional associations, neighborhood organizations, and community institutions that high-income, college-educated residents rely on for civic engagement; a 64-point margin is won by presence and responsiveness, not by partisan advantage alone."
