          { name: "Defaulting to Majority-White Homeowner Concerns as Sufficient District Strategy", tag: "avoid", why: "A district where 70% are white and 79% own homes can easily default to a legislative agenda focused on property taxes, school property values, and homeowner-specific concerns — and in an unopposed context, that strategy produces no visible political cost. However, it leaves 28%+ of residents and their specific economic and social concerns unaddressed in the public record, creating an opening for a challenger to position themselves as serving the entire district. In an affluent, educated constituency, this kind of representational blind spot is both ethically problematic and strategically risky." }
