          { name: "Conflating Democratic Registration with Ideological Homogeneity", tag: "avoid", why: "The complete Democratic monopoly on representation masks real ideological and policy diversity within a highly educated urban constituency: disagreements on housing development, transportation priorities, school funding, immigration enforcement, and police reform exist across the Democratic spectrum and deserve representation that acknowledges these tensions rather than presenting a single ideological perspective as inevitable. An unopposed representative who assumes Democratic registration means ideological alignment risks developing a constituency relationship based on passive loyalty rather than active engagement with the specific priorities of the people who actually live here." }
