          "Engage the Asian community with specific constituent attention and community-based representation: at 20.49%, Asian residents are the second-largest demographic group and represent significant civic participation, educational achievement, and economic contribution that deserves proportional representation in constituent services, committee assignments, and legislative priority-setting rather than being absorbed into generic 'community' framing.",
          "Make education cost accessibility a concrete legislative agenda, not an abstract value: with 71.7% college education and a median age of 32.4, this is a district of parents navigating childcare costs, student loan debt, and early-childhood education affordability — real budget items for young families earning $114,840 in a high-cost urban market.",
