          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency on service delivery and policy substance: at 84% college-educated and median age 30.2, this district evaluates representatives on whether legislative and constituent service actually work, whether healthcare access is viable, and whether the state is delivering on infrastructure and quality-of-life commitments — not inherited partisan loyalty or abstract ideological positioning.",
          "Maintain active constituent service infrastructure in a high-mobility district: the 73% renter rate and urban location mean significant cohort turnover; any incumbent must assume 20-25% of the electorate is new to the district in each election cycle and requires genuine outreach, not passive reliance on party registration.",
          "Do not assume the unopposed 2024 result reflects durable coalition strength: 100% Democratic in a district with meaningful demographic diversity and a young, mobile, renter-majority constituency is a partisan result, not a mandate; the absence of Republican opposition in 2024 does not mean future challengers will lack a persuadable electorate around housing, healthcare, or public service delivery."
