          "Lead with housing affordability and renter protections: with nearly 70% of the district renting at median household incomes that make housing cost burden acute, anti-displacement initiatives, tenant rights enforcement, and affordable housing development are the most tangible ways to consolidate the Latino-majority base and demonstrate attentiveness to the material concerns driving electoral behavior.",
          "Engage the 21% White, 7.6% Black, and 2.96% Asian populations with specific constituent attention and service delivery rather than assuming they will remain passive; in a young (34.3 median age), diverse working-class district, these communities' economic mobility and service-access concerns deserve direct policy focus, and neglecting them creates openings for primary challengers.",
          "Build visible, ongoing constituent service infrastructure — public office hours, mobile constituent service clinics, multilingual constituent staff, and responsive case management for housing, benefits, and healthcare access — as the foundation for electoral durability; unopposed incumbents are vulnerable to challengers who can credibly claim superior responsiveness, and active constituent service is the inoculation against that challenge."
