          { name: "Assuming Inherited Partisan Loyalty Among Young, Educated, Diverse Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "This district's 33.5 median age, 63.9% college attainment, and 50-50 racial diversity together signal a politically sophisticated constituency that evaluates on specific policy delivery and constituent responsiveness, not party affiliation. An incumbent who assumes that young professionals, renters, and non-white communities will vote Democratic by default — rather than actively demonstrating material delivery on housing, economic opportunity, and racial equity — creates opening for a challenger who offers concrete answers to the concerns that actually shape how this constituency votes." }
