          { name: "Treating High Income ($93,913 median) as Equivalent to Constituent Affluence or Stability", tag: "avoid", why: "While $93,913 median household income is well above state average, in Boston's housing market and cost-of-living environment it is insufficient for homeownership, childcare affordability, or economic security for a young renter-majority constituency. A representative who frames this district as affluent and therefore content, rather than as credential-holding professionals materially constrained by metro-area costs, misreads the constituent experience. This error invites a challenger to occupy the space between credential and economic reality, speaking directly to the gap between educational achievement and material security that defines the district's lived experience." }
