          { name: "Conflating Generic 'Working Families' Messaging with Community-Specific Constituent Attention", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district with three distinct demographic communities—28.7% Latino, 6.75% Black, and 57.98% white—all with different material concerns and economic positions, an incumbent who defaults to abstract 'working families' messaging misses the specific policy commitments and constituent relationships that generate durable support. The Latino community needs visible action on wage floors and workplace protections; the renter majority needs visible action on housing affordability; the Black community needs visible institutional engagement on policing and economic access. A representative who treats these as sub-categories of a unified constituency rather than as distinct communities with specific needs will discover that the opposition can outperform in the seats that matter most." }
