          "Engage the 17.14% Latino population with specific policy wins and community relationships, not generic appeals: economic mobility in a high-cost district, healthcare access, education quality, and immigrant family protection are the issues that activate Latino voter participation and determine whether that 17% turns out and votes for the incumbent or sits home.",
          "Build durable relationships with working-class homeowners in the 37.1% renter / 62.9% homeowner mix: a 57% result is not a supermajority, and any candidate who assumes homeowner loyalty rather than delivering on affordability, service quality, and municipal fiscal responsibility risks seeing that constituency shift toward a Republican challenger who promises tax relief and efficiency."
