          { name: "Neglecting White and Black Minority Communities in a Latino-Majority Engagement Framework", tag: "avoid", why: "While Hispanic/Latino residents comprise the largest demographic group at 30.36%, the 45.61% white and 11.19% Black populations are substantial communities whose economic concerns and service expectations cannot be absorbed into generic majority-community outreach. Working-class white renters and Black residents face similar cost-of-living and healthcare access constraints as Hispanic/Latino households, and a representative who focuses exclusively on the largest demographic group while rendering other constituencies politically invisible will find those communities unengaged or receptive to alternative candidates. Specific constituent service and policy attention to all working-class communities in the district is more electorally durable than demographic-targeting frameworks that implicitly rank some constituencies as primary and others as secondary." }
