          { name: "Overlooking the District's Only Meaningful Growth Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "The 6-7% combined Hispanic and Asian population is small but likely concentrated in specific towns and represents the only meaningful demographic growth in a district that is 80.26% white with a 41.7 median age. An incumbent or challenger who focuses exclusively on the white homeowner majority and treats the Hispanic and Asian communities as peripheral constituencies is both failing to build a forward-looking coalition and missing the actual demographic trends that will define the district in ten years. Specific attention to economic mobility, education access, and workforce development for these communities is both a governance obligation and an electoral necessity." }
