          "MA Senate Bristol-Norfolk is among the most decisively Democratic districts in Massachusetts, with Feeney capturing 73% in 2024 against 27% Republican opposition. The district's demographic profile explains this result with clarity: 50.6% college-educated adults, $114,989 median household income, 78.99% white, and a 41.4-year median age all point to an affluent suburban constituency with high educational attainment and economic security. The 26.4% renter rate indicates a homeowner-dominant base, but one integrated with professional workers and educated young families for whom quality of life, educational investment, and governance competence are primary voting criteria. The 73-27 result is not a landslide driven by partisan enthusiasm — it is a professional-class mandate reflecting alignment between the district's material interests and Democratic governance on education funding, fiscal responsibility, and quality-of-life infrastructure.",
