          "Housing affordability for young professionals and mid-career families is the vulnerability in an otherwise stable district: $114,989 income is strong, but it does not go as far in Massachusetts housing markets as it did ten years ago. A candidate who addresses the genuine constraint on housing access for the district's educated young families addresses a material quality-of-life issue that transcends partisan lines."
