          { name: "Consolidating Only the Affluent Homeowner Base While Neglecting Renter & Younger-Adult Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "The 53.7-year median age and high homeownership create a natural Democratic base, but the 21.3% renter rate and working-class service-sector constituency represent real economic concerns separate from the affluent homeowner majority. Any representative who campaigns as though they can consolidate only the older, asset-holding base and neglect younger and working-class constituents is strategically error-prone — these secondary constituencies can organize credible alternatives if they conclude the incumbent is not serving their economic security. Active engagement with the full breadth of the district is both a governance obligation and an electoral necessity." }
