          { name: "Treating the Latino Majority as a Monolithic Base Without Ongoing Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "The 61.14% Latino population is not a guaranteed Democratic vote—it is a constituency that evaluates on economic results, responsive constituent service, and whether elected officials deliver concrete improvements in housing, wages, and healthcare. Latino voters in working-class districts with high renter rates are capable of supporting different candidates and parties if they believe their economic concerns are not being addressed. Any incumbent who consolidates only the existing Democratic coalition without actively demonstrating economic impact for Latino renters risks finding that coalition more fragile than the unopposed victory suggests." }
