          "Engage the young professional constituency on delivery and problem-solving: the 33.8 median age and 67.4% college attainment signal a constituency that expects competence, measurable progress on stated priorities, and responsiveness to constituent needs. An incumbent who has not visibly delivered on housing, childcare, or wage-growth issues, or who is perceived as distant or unresponsive, faces a credible vulnerability from a challenger who can demonstrate a track record of problem-solving.",
          "Avoid writing off the educated, affluent constituency as culturally locked-in Democratic: high income and education correlate with political independence and cross-partisan persuadability on economic substance, not with tribal Democratic loyalty. Young professionals in the $129k median income range with high education evaluate on governance performance, not inherited partisan preference.",
          "Treat the unopposed 2024 result as a warning signal, not reassurance: the absence of Republican opposition in a district with this demographic profile suggests weak recruitment or strategic dismissal of the seat as inaccessible, not proof that it is actually safe. A credible challenger with a coherent economic message tailored to young renters' material constraints could activate latent persuadability and expose the incumbent to genuine competitive pressure."
