          { name: "Treating Demographic Advantage as Substitute for Constituent Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "High income, high education, and substantial professional networks do not automatically translate into constituent satisfaction with or loyalty to an incumbent. Prosperous, well-educated constituencies often have higher expectations for responsive constituent service, specific legislative accomplishment, and alignment with their material interests — not lower ones. An incumbent who relies on demographic advantage to compensate for weak constituent engagement or generic Democratic messaging will find that advantage insufficient when a credible alternative emerges." }
