          "Lead on housing affordability and renter protections: In a district where six-in-ten residents rent and the median age is 35.5, housing cost burden is the primary quality-of-life concern. Specific policies on rent regulation, tenant protections, affordable housing development, and the relationship between housing costs and young professionals' economic mobility are non-negotiable constituent engagement issues.",
