          { name: "Partisan Complacency from Unopposed Status", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed 2024 result is a gift, not a baseline. In a district this demographically competitive — 69% minority, 68.5% renters at $65,532 income — the absence of organized opposition does not indicate electoral safety; it indicates an incumbent with sufficient standing to deter challengers. That standing is contingent on active constituent service, not inherited. Any representative who interprets unopposed status as permission to reduce engagement with the renter, young adult, and minority communities will create the opening for a credible challenger in the next cycle." },
          { name: "Treating Minority Communities as Constituency Service Afterthoughts", tag: "avoid", why: "With 42.78% Black and 26.02% Hispanic residents comprising nearly 70% of the district, these communities are not a minority to be accommodated — they are the constituency core. Any representative whose legislative record, rhetoric, or constituent service infrastructure treats Black and Hispanic constituents as separate from the 'main' constituency, or whose economic development agenda focuses on sectors that do not employ or serve these communities, will find that positioning actively hostile to the demographic reality of who lives in the district." }
