          "Diagnose the 41% Republican share in a $136k-income district as a specific strategic problem: identify whether it reflects economic anxiety among professionals around tax policy and fiscal management, cultural alienation from progressive social positions, or messaging failure that leaves educated voters skeptical of Democratic competence. Address the actual concern, not the partisan label.",
          "Engage the 24.9% renter constituency with specific housing-affordability policy rather than assuming all renters are young and all homeowners are conservative: renters in a $136k-median-income district include young professionals, service workers, and others whose housing economics differ materially from the majority homeowner population and represent both a demographic fact and a latent electoral opportunity.",
