          "Lead on housing policy with specificity: in a 51.4% renter-majority district with $76,260 median income, housing affordability is not a side issue—it is the primary economic fact of most constituents' lives. Tenant protections, affordable housing development, and rent stabilization are the concrete policy agenda that differentiates an incumbent who is genuinely serving renters from one who is taking them for granted.",
